# Copy this file to .env and fill in your own values.
#   cp .env.example .env
# .env is git-ignored and must never be committed.
#
# The file has to exist for the app to build, because pubspec.yaml lists it as
# an asset — that is how flutter_dotenv reads it. An empty .env is fine.

# --- NEVER ship or deploy ----------------------------------------------------
# Gemini powers Nook's destination, category, summary and coordinate detection.
# The key is billable: anyone can read a value compiled into a web build and
# spend your quota, so it is deliberately NOT a repository secret and never
# reaches the deployed site.
#
# Leave this blank and Nook falls back to its sample extractor, which is exactly
# what the published GitHub Pages build does — and it says so on screen.
# Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional. Leave blank and Nook asks the API which models your key can reach
# and picks the cheapest one that fits (a flash-lite tier). Set an id here only
# to pin a specific model, e.g. gemini-flash-lite-latest.
GEMINI_MODEL=
